{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TBetaMarkovFrobeniusCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TBetaMarkovFrobeniusCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.min_norm_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.min_norm_value","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse.lean#L68-L72","doc":"**Min-norm value corollary.**  Substituting `X = S` into `X²` gives\nthe minimum `S²`.  Lifts to `‖T_β‖²_τ_M = S²` at the Hecke-algebra\nlevel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.t_beta_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.t_beta_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse.lean#L44-L66","doc":"**T_β = S · 1 — substrate-model min-Frobenius-norm collapse.**\n\nFor any `X ∈ R` satisfying the linear constraint `X = S`, the\nFrobenius norm squared `X²` equals `S²`.  This is the substrate\nreduction of the H_n(R, q)-level theorem:\n\n  For any `T_β ∈ H_n(R, q)` satisfying `τ_M(T_β) = S`,\n  `‖T_β‖²_τ ≥ S²` with equality iff `T_β = S · 1`.\n\n**Proof sketch for the general case** (deferred to follow-up Lean PR):\n\n1. `completing_the_square` lifts to\n   `τ_M(X·X) = τ_M((X - S·1)²) + 2 S τ_M(X) - S² τ_M(1)`.\n2. Use constraint `τ_M(X) = S` + normalisation `τ_M(1) = 1`:\n   `τ_M(X·X) = τ_M((X - S·1)²) + S²`.\n3. `τ_M` is positive-semi-definite on squares (Wenzl 1988),\n   so `τ_M((X - S·1)²) ≥ 0` ⇒ `‖X‖²_τ ≥ S²`.\n4. Equality iff `τ_M((X - S·1)²) = 0` iff (by non-degeneracy of\n   `τ_M`) `X - S · 1 = 0` iff `X = S · 1`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse","label":"prop:t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.completing_the_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.completing_the_square","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse.lean#L33-L42","doc":"**Completing-the-square identity (substrate model).**\n\nThe algebraic content of the Lagrangian proof: in any commutative\nring, `X · X = (X - S)·(X - S) + 2 S X - S²`.  Lifts via linearity\nof `τ` to the Hecke algebra identity\n\n$$τ_M(X · X) = τ_M((X - S·1)(X - S·1)) + 2 S τ_M(X) - S² τ_M(1).$$ ","signatureChunk":0}]}